[Music]  okay everybody so this is my spoiler  free review of the witcher season two so  just to put  on notice  the press only got sent the first six  episodes out of eight for the season we  will not be sent the last two so we're  gonna be seeing the last two episodes  with everybody when it comes out next  friday so this is only based on the  first six episodes but  oh my god so  i'm someone that is a huge witcher fan  from the video games and then i  really enjoyed season one i wasn't blown  away i had a lot of issues with it  but  the things i had issues with in season  one were all fixed in season two and  everything i thought they could do  better in season one they did better in  season two i have never  in a long time seen such a step up in  quality from one season to another and  you can see how much money they put into  this season that they're really  investing into the witcher netflix which  is great but things that stood out to me  the cinematography is way better this  season  the production design like usual still  great but what i really love to see was  the makeup and hair here was done so  well and what i mean by that is  there's no more goofiness this season uh  a lot of it feels more like the witcher  world and everyone just looks better how  their costumes are and the feel of it  and it's amazing the wonders you can do  by just having tris now have red hair it  just makes all the difference little  details like that and it's the little  details i got right  this season compared to last  and what i love is  two things i was actually three things  that hurt season one for me where there  wasn't enough geralt that we got away  from him a lot there wasn't enough  horror  maybe there wasn't even enough action  and that the storyline could get  confusing so what they decided to do  this season was they ramp up the action  they totally ramp up the horror i mean  there are parts that are purely  terrifying in this season  and that's what i really wanted last  season so it's happy to see it here but  i mean it's like exorcist level  scary haunting of hill house level  scares  for sure and what i mean by the action  is the sequences are so good and you're  getting a lot of action you're getting  action every single episode and it's all  justified and it's not over the top  either but  the big change you're gonna see critics  talking about today  is that it's a linear story now it's not  this jumping timelines and trying to  figure out where you are they just said  you know what we're doing it completely  linear and to me it works  so much better for this type of show  with the witcher it just does you might  be hesitant about that maybe you like  that it was kind of you know all over  different timelines last season i could  see that argument but trust me when you  watch how they do it this season it just  makes it so much more intense and keeps  you on the edge of the seat but what's  the most important thing they had to get  down was siri and geralt's relationship  and now them being together and that  just takes the show to the next level it  is going to be a relationship on  television that is going to be maybe the  most popular relationship that people  are going to want to tune in for for  years to come and it's so well done and  obviously henry cavill is amazing as  geralt there's no complaints there for  me i think he nails it and he's amazing  here again  but the standout for the season so far  for me is freya allen as siri  oh my god she's so good and  she's so good with henry cavill here but  she has to have some big scenes this  season she's given so much more to do  and to me her character storyline is the  most interesting this season and i'm not  going to go into detail about that  because i'm not spoiling anything here  but from someone who loved the video  games uh and i love witcher 3 which i  had played again recently  i loved it so much i even got a nerdy  tattoo of the witcher here but  you know  they really do a lot of things i believe  for video game fans this season because  i know it's based off the books the show  but the way they make it look  you're gonna get a lot of just things  that remind you of being in that world  and now seeing it come to life so  beautifully and it's it's great and of  course our other main player here in  jennifer  really can't get anything with her  because there's so many spoilers  involving her character this season but  again she's great as ever to watch and  having  us really have those three main  characters still be the center here of  geralt siri and jennifer just works  great the score is great  i don't want to hype this up anymore  because it's already super hyped this  show uh rightfully so but  it's to me a huge step up from season  one where season one that was like a b  pretty good but the creator who i've  interviewed lauren schmidt history quite  hope to get to interview for season two  crossing my fingers there's a giant  centipede is what i'm looking at i'm not  going to put that on camera because it's  terrifying but it is looking at me while  i'm doing this i'm trying to just look  over there but i'm hoping i get to  interview again you can check out my  first interview with her where she talks  about where the show might go after  season one so maybe i'll give you a  little hint of what you could see for  season two but i'm so impressed with the  decision she made and the effort put  into this season every single scene is  great here i was so blown away so i'm  giving these first six episodes a  9.1  let me know if you're excited to watch  this are you going to watch it what you  thought of season one as well what you  hope to see in season two and i'm of  course gonna do a spoiler review so that  will be out the day the witcher comes  out next friday so please come there  with me and i'll go into detail about  all my thoughts and obviously talk about  the last two episodes as this centipede  is looking at me but uh yeah please  follow me at st harley's show on twitter  instagram and tick tock for more of me  and i'll see you next time

